                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_2",
          "subsection_title": "Introduction and definition",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_2",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A surgical stapler is a medical device used to join, close, or divide tissues using specially designed metal staples. Some staplers also incorporate a blade to cut tissue between or alongside staple lines."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "They provide a consistent method of tissue approximation and haemostasis and are widely used in gastrointestinal, thoracic, gynaecological and other surgical procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Key OSCE distinction: A surgical stapler is not the same as a skin stapler. A surgical stapler is designed for internal tissue, anastomosis or organ transection, whereas a skin stapler is designed primarily for external skin closure."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_3",
          "subsection_title": "Identification and general features",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_3",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/surgical_stapler_03.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Identification: Surgical stapler."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Characteristic features"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Handle or firing mechanism."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Jaws that hold the tissue or tissue structures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Staple cartridge containing preloaded staples."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Anvil or opposing jaw that shapes the staples."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Safety lock or firing interlock on many models."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Some models contain a cutting blade."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Disposable or reusable components, depending on the device."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Stapler designs differ considerably. In an OSCE, identify the actual type shown rather than assuming every stapler has a blade, circular anvil or reloadable cartridge."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_4",
          "subsection_title": "Labelling and parts",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_4",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/surgical_stapler_04.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "roussurgical.cz"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Part",
                    "Function"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Handle/grip",
                      "Allows the operator to hold and control the device."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Trigger or firing mechanism",
                      "Deploys the staples when correctly activated."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Jaws",
                      "Position and compress the target tissue."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Staple cartridge",
                      "Holds the staples before firing."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Anvil",
                      "Shapes the staples into their intended configuration."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Cutting blade, where present",
                      "Divides tissue as part of the firing sequence."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Tissue-gap adjustment, where available",
                      "Helps select an appropriate tissue-compression setting."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Safety interlock",
                      "Helps prevent unintended or inappropriate firing."
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The cartridge and anvil may be incorporated differently in linear, circular and skin staplers."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_5",
          "subsection_title": "Classification of surgical staplers",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_5",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Surgical staplers are classified according to their design and intended function."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/surgical_stapler_05.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "A. Linear stapler"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Places one or more parallel rows of staples without necessarily cutting the tissue."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Uses: Closing or dividing selected hollow organs and tissues, depending on the specific model."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/surgical_stapler_06.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "B. Linear cutting stapler"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Places staple rows on either side of a cutting line while dividing tissue."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Uses: Bowel transection, creation of anastomoses, gastric procedures and selected thoracic operations."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/surgical_stapler_07.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "C. Circular stapler"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Places a circular staple line and usually removes a circular tissue core."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Uses: Selected end-to-end or end-to-side anastomoses, including colorectal and oesophageal anastomoses."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/surgical_stapler_08.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "D. Specialised staplers"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Include vascular staplers, thoracic staplers and other devices designed for specific tissues, access routes or surgical tasks."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Other useful classifications include:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Open surgical staplers: Used directly in an operative field."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Endoscopic/laparoscopic staplers: Introduced through a compatible minimally invasive access port."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Powered staplers: Use a motorised firing mechanism."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Manual staplers: Use a hand-operated firing mechanism."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_6",
          "subsection_title": "Principle of operation",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_6",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Most surgical staplers use a cartridge and an opposing anvil to form staples into a predetermined shape, commonly a B-shaped configuration."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The general sequence is:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The tissue is positioned between the jaws."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The jaws approximate and compress the tissue according to the device's design."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The operator verifies that the intended tissue is correctly positioned and that the device is suitable for its thickness."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The stapler is fired according to the manufacturer's instructions."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Staples are deployed and shaped by the anvil."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Where applicable, an integrated blade divides tissue between the staple lines."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The device is released and the completed staple line is inspected for integrity and bleeding."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Important principle: Correct staple formation depends on appropriate tissue thickness, cartridge selection, compression, device positioning and complete firing. The exact sequence varies between stapler designs."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_7",
          "subsection_title": "Common surgical applications",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_7",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Specialty/procedure",
                    "Role of surgical stapler"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Bowel resection",
                      "Closes or divides bowel and may facilitate anastomosis."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Colorectal surgery",
                      "Creates selected colorectal anastomoses, often using a circular stapler."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Gastric surgery",
                      "Divides or closes stomach tissue in selected procedures."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Oesophageal surgery",
                      "Facilitates selected oesophageal or gastrointestinal anastomoses."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Thoracic surgery",
                      "Divides lung tissue or closes selected bronchial structures with compatible devices."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Vascular surgery",
                      "Specialised devices may be used to close or divide selected vessels."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Laparoscopic surgery",
                      "Allows tissue division, closure or anastomosis through minimally invasive access."
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The appropriate device depends on the anatomy, tissue thickness, surgical technique and the manufacturer's approved indications."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_8",
          "subsection_title": "Advantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_8",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Rapid tissue closure and division."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Consistent staple formation when used correctly."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "May shorten operative time in selected procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Can facilitate minimally invasive surgery."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Can create reproducible staple lines."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Some designs allow simultaneous tissue division and stapling."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Can be useful when hand suturing is difficult in confined operative spaces."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_9",
          "subsection_title": "Disadvantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_9",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "More expensive than many conventional suturing techniques."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Requires appropriate cartridge selection and familiarity with the device."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Incorrect positioning or incomplete firing can compromise the staple line."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Not suitable for every tissue type, thickness or anatomical location."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "May require additional suturing or haemostatic measures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Staple lines may be difficult to revise if a technical error occurs."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Some devices generate disposable waste and have limited reuse options."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_10",
          "subsection_title": "Complications",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_10",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/surgical_stapler_09.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "A. Staple-line leakage"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Failure of the staple line to seal adequately may cause leakage of gastrointestinal contents, peritonitis or sepsis, depending on the anatomical site."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/surgical_stapler_10.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "B. Bleeding"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Inadequate staple formation, tissue injury or failure to control bleeding may lead to postoperative haemorrhage."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/surgical_stapler_11.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "C. Anastomotic stricture"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Scar formation and healing complications can narrow an anastomosis, potentially causing obstruction or impaired passage."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "D. Technical failure"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Misfiring, incomplete firing, staple malformation, cartridge problems or failure to release the device can compromise the procedure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Other complications include tissue tearing, injury to adjacent structures, retained or misplaced staples, infection, and damage caused by inappropriate compression or cartridge selection."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_11",
          "subsection_title": "Safety precautions and handling",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_11",
              "group_title": "Before use",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Confirm the correct stapler type, cartridge and intended tissue."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Inspect the packaging, sterility, expiry date and device integrity."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Check compatibility between the stapler and cartridge."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Ensure that the tissue thickness falls within the manufacturer's specifications."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Position the tissue correctly and ensure that unintended structures are not trapped between the jaws."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_12",
              "group_title": "During use",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Follow the manufacturer's instructions for tissue compression and firing."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Do not force a trigger or attempt to override a safety mechanism."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If firing resistance or a malfunction occurs, stop and follow the device-specific troubleshooting procedure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Avoid blind firing where adjacent structures may be at risk."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_13",
              "group_title": "After firing",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Inspect the staple line for bleeding, tissue injury and integrity."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Assess the anastomosis using the appropriate technique for the procedure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Confirm that the device has released correctly."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Manage any staple-line defect according to surgical findings."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Dispose of single-use devices or process reusable components according to their instructions."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_12",
          "subsection_title": "Surgical stapler versus skin stapler",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_14",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Feature",
                    "Surgical stapler",
                    "Skin stapler"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Primary purpose",
                      "Internal tissue closure, division or anastomosis",
                      "External skin closure"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Design",
                      "Linear, circular, cutting or specialised configurations",
                      "Usually a handheld applicator with a small staple cartridge"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Staple formation",
                      "Depends on the tissue-specific cartridge and anvil",
                      "Staples approximate skin edges"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Common applications",
                      "Bowel resection, anastomosis, selected thoracic procedures",
                      "Closure of suitable surgical incisions and lacerations"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Main risks",
                      "Leakage, bleeding, tissue injury and technical failure",
                      "Skin-edge separation, poor cosmetic outcome, infection and staple-related skin injury"
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Exam pearl: A circular stapler is frequently used to create an anastomosis, whereas a skin stapler is used to approximate the external skin edges."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_13",
          "subsection_title": "High-yield OSCE viva questions",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_15",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q1. What is a surgical stapler?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A device used to approximate, close or divide tissues using specially designed staples. Some models also cut tissue."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q2. What is the difference between a linear and a circular stapler?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A linear stapler creates straight staple lines, while a circular stapler creates a ring-shaped staple line and is commonly used for selected gastrointestinal anastomoses."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q3. What is a linear cutting stapler?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A stapler that deploys staple rows while an integrated blade divides tissue between or alongside the staple lines, according to the design."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q4. What are the major complications of gastrointestinal stapling?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Staple-line bleeding, leakage, anastomotic stricture, tissue injury and technical failure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q5. Why is cartridge selection important?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Staple cartridges are designed for particular tissue thicknesses and applications. An inappropriate cartridge can result in inadequate compression or staple formation and compromise tissue integrity."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q6. What would you do if the stapler fails to fire?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Stop, maintain control of the operative field, avoid forcing or repeatedly activating the mechanism, and follow the manufacturer's troubleshooting instructions. The surgeon should use an appropriate alternative or conversion strategy if necessary."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q7. Why might a surgeon choose stapling over suturing?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Stapling can provide rapid, reproducible tissue closure and facilitate selected minimally invasive procedures. The choice depends on the tissue, anatomy, clinical circumstances and surgeon's judgement."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_14",
          "subsection_title": "High-yield examination tips",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_16",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Identify the exact type of stapler: linear, linear cutting, circular or specialised."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Label the handle, trigger, jaws, cartridge, anvil and blade where present."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Explain the B-shaped staple formation principle."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Know that some staplers cut tissue while others only staple."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Mention gastrointestinal anastomosis as a major application."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Prioritise staple-line leakage and bleeding among complications."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Explain the importance of tissue thickness and correct cartridge selection."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Never confuse an internal surgical stapler with a skin stapler."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "surgical_stapler_subsection_15",
          "subsection_title": "Model OSCE presentation",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "surgical_stapler_group_17",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "“This is a surgical stapler, a device used to approximate, close or divide tissues using surgical staples. Depending on its design, it may be linear, linear cutting, circular or specialised. Its components include the handle, firing mechanism, jaws, staple cartridge and anvil, with an integrated blade in cutting models. It is used in procedures such as bowel resection, gastrointestinal anastomosis and selected thoracic operations. Advantages include speed and reproducibility. Complications include staple-line bleeding, leakage, stricture, tissue injury and technical failure.”"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}